# Home screen widget — iOS setup

`chameleon create --home-widget` generated the Android widget fully
working out of the box. iOS can't be automated the same way — Apple gives
no scriptable path for creating a Widget Extension target, only Xcode's
own UI (confirmed against Flutter's own
["Adding iOS app extensions"](https://docs.flutter.dev/platform-integration/ios/app-extensions)
doc and `home_widget`'s setup docs). This folder holds the Swift source
ready to drop into that target once you create it — do the following once,
by hand:

1. Open `ios/Runner.xcworkspace` in Xcode.
2. **File > New > Target… > Widget Extension.** Name it
   `ChameleonHomeWidget`. Uncheck "Include Configuration App Intent" (this
   widget isn't user-configurable). Uncheck "Include Live Activity" too.
3. Xcode generates its own starter Swift file for the new target — delete
   it, then drag `ChameleonHomeWidget.swift` from this folder into the new
   target (make sure "Copy items if needed" and the `ChameleonHomeWidget`
   target membership are both checked).
4. **App Groups**, needed so the main app and the widget can share data:
   - In your [Apple Developer Account](https://developer.account.apple.com),
     under Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles > Identifiers > App Groups,
     register a new group with the identifier
     `group.{{org_name}}.{{project_name.snakeCase()}}.homewidget` — this
     exact string, since it's already baked into both
     `ChameleonHomeWidget.swift` (this folder) and
     `lib/core/home_widget/home_widget_updater_impl.dart`.
   - Back in Xcode, select the **Runner** target > Signing & Capabilities >
     **+ Capability** > App Groups, add the group above, and repeat for the
     **ChameleonHomeWidget** target (the target dropdown at the top of the
     editor switches between them).
5. Build and run. The widget starts showing "No title set"/"No value set"
   until something in the app calls
   `getIt<HomeWidgetUpdater>().saveData('title', ...)` /
   `.saveData('value', ...)` followed by `.updateWidget()`.

Nothing above is checked by `tool/checks.sh` — there's no reliable
text-based way to verify "a Widget Extension target exists," unlike a
missing `Info.plist` key. Long-press the home screen and confirm
`ChameleonHomeWidget` appears in the widget gallery as your own
verification.
